Built a dashboard to replicate how a FICC desk frames risk before taking duration or curve exposure.

The focus is not forecasting, but identifying when moves in the 10Y and key curve spreads (3m10y, 5s10s, 10s30s) are coherent, accelerating, or breaking down. A rolling heatmap and a single curve acceleration score make it clear whether the market is repricing policy, term premium, or transitioning regimes.
This is the type of tool used to decide when to press risk, when to step back, and when relative value is safer than direction.
